Helios DXVK fork: D3D11.1 target-independent rasterization on mixed samples

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0016 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

Direct2D fills complex geometry (the Windows 11 shell's vector icons) with
target-independent rasterization: ForcedSampleCount 16 in a rasterizer state
made with CreateRasterizerState1, a single-sample render target, and a pixel
shader that derives its alpha from the covered samples in SV_Coverage. DXVK
dropped ForcedSampleCount from D3D11_RASTERIZER_DESC1 (only the DESC2 path
kept it) and took the rasterization sample count from the render targets
whenever one was bound, so those draws rasterized at one sample and every
covered pixel got 1/16 of its coverage (guest/windows/tools/d2d_tir_probe.cpp:
maximum alpha 16 instead of 255).

- D3D11RasterizerState::PromoteDesc(D3D11_RASTERIZER_DESC1) keeps
  ForcedSampleCount, as the DESC2 path does.
- One rule decides the rasterization sample count, dxvkRasterizationSamples()
  with the device's DxvkRasterizationSampleCaps: the render targets' count;
  without render targets (UAV-only rendering) the rasterizer state's count,
  limited to the largest count in framebufferNoAttachmentsSampleCounts (D3D11
  allows ForcedSampleCount 16 there, NVK rasterizes at most 8 without
  attachments); and with VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples (NVK on Maxwell B+)
  the rasterizer state's count when it is above the render targets' and no
  depth-stencil target is bound (D3D forbids one with a forced sample count).
  The pipeline's multisample state, the dynamic rasterization samples, the
  sample locations and the D3D11 rasterizer sample count specialization
  constant (sampleinfo / samplepos on the rasterizer, now also updated when a
  depth-stencil view is bound or unbound) all use it, so shaders see the count
  the rasterizer runs at.
- Vulkan does not allow sample rate shading with mixed samples, and D3D
  leaves sample-frequency shading undefined under a forced sample count: such
  pipelines shade per pixel instead, so the rule does not depend on the
  shaders. Fast-linked pipelines from libraries, whose fragment shader
  library enables sample rate shading, are not used for them.
- Mixed-samples pipelines chain VkAttachmentSampleCountInfoAMD with the render
  targets' sample count (dynamic rendering assumes the rasterization sample
  count otherwise), which is part of the fragment output state's key.

Without the extension, or with sample counts that match, the rasterization
sample count is what it was, except for UAV-only rendering above the device's
limit.

